+*   **Input:** A sequence of volume datasets $V_t$ for time steps $t = 0, \dots, N-1$. Each $V_t$ is a 3D grid of voxels [S1, S2, unofficial].
 *   **Output:** A compressed, merged octree structure (compositing tree) that enables selective rendering with reduced computational cost [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
 ### Data Structures
 The core data structure is an octree where each node represents a block of voxels [S1, S2, unofficial].
-*   **Leaf Node:** Represents a uniform block of voxels. Stores the representative quantized value and transparency metadata [S1, S2, unofficial].
-*   **Internal Node:** Represents a subdivision of space. Contains pointers to its eight children [S1, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Leaf Node:** Represents a uniform block of voxels [S1, S2, unofficial]. Stores the representative quantized value and transparency metadata [S1, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Internal Node:** Represents a subdivision of space [S1, S2, unofficial]. Contains pointers to its eight children [S1, S2, unofficial].
 *   **Tree Merging:** If the octree structure and voxel values of a subtree at time $t$ are identical to the corresponding subtree at time $t-1$, the subtree at $t$ is merged with $t-1$ [S1, S2, unofficial].
 *   **Minimum Renderable Block:** The renderer is configured to stop at a minimum depth, corresponding to an 8-voxel block [S1, S2, unofficial]. Nodes smaller than this (1-voxel or 8-voxel merges) are not useful for rendering performance gains because a single voxel change forces re-rendering of surrounding voxels [S1, S2, unofficial].
