 ## Background
-The method was developed for the 'twd-renderer' for time-varying volume data visualization [S2, unofficial]. It builds on the concept of using octree compression to fit multiple timesteps into main memory, overcoming GPU memory and bus bandwidth limitations [Parent]. The technique was presented in a 1998 NASA Technical Report and DTIC document [S1, S2, unofficial]. The research demonstrated that combining spatial compression (octree) and temporal compression (tree merging) could achieve tremendous savings in storage and rendering time, justifying interactive visualization of time-varying data [S1, S2, unofficial].
+The method was developed for the 'twd-renderer' for time-varying volume data visualization [S2, unofficial]. It builds on the concept of using octree compression to fit multiple timesteps into main memory, overcoming GPU memory and bus bandwidth limitations [Time-Variant Volume Rendering with Octrees](2232-time-variant-volume-rendering-with-octrees.md). The technique was presented in a 1998 NASA Technical Report and DTIC document [S1, S2, unofficial]. The research demonstrated that combining spatial compression (octree) and temporal compression (tree merging) could achieve tremendous savings in storage and rendering time, justifying interactive visualization of time-varying data [S1, S2, unofficial].
 
